WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.612 --> 00:00:05.657
♪ ♪

2
00:00:11.141 --> 00:00:13.404
<i>[slow. heavy breathing]</i>

3
00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:27.027
♪ ♪

4
00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:38.734
<i>[slow. heavy breathing
continues]</i>

5
00:00:50.137 --> 00:00:52.835
<i>[breathing intensifies]</i>

6
00:00:52.878 --> 00:00:54.924
♪ ♪

7
00:01:17.512 --> 00:01:19.514
[slow. heavy breathing]

8
00:01:23.474 --> 00:01:25.520
♪ ♪

9
00:01:34.181 --> 00:01:36.183
[heavy breathing continues]

10
00:01:55.289 --> 00:01:56.551
[moans softly]

11
00:01:56.594 --> 00:01:59.597
[mechanical whirring]

12
00:01:59.641 --> 00:02:02.600
[slow beeping]

13
00:02:05.647 --> 00:02:08.780
[beeping growing faster]

14
00:02:13.089 --> 00:02:15.657
[short. rapid breaths]

15
00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:16.919
[choking]

16
00:02:16.962 --> 00:02:18.094
Stop.

17
00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:19.965
-[rapid beeping]
-Too much.

18
00:02:20.009 --> 00:02:21.184
[choking]

19
00:02:21.228 --> 00:02:22.664
Get her off me.

20
00:02:25.362 --> 00:02:28.017
-[heavy breathing]
-[choking continues]

21
00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:29.497
[electronic trilling]

22
00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:30.759
[gasping breaths]

23
00:02:32.543 --> 00:02:34.545
♪ ♪

24
00:02:38.549 --> 00:02:42.684
CEO: <i>At Ultima Robotix.
we thrive on connection.</i>

25
00:02:42.727 --> 00:02:46.035
<i>We started with Elsie.
your favorite home assistant.</i>

26
00:02:46.078 --> 00:02:48.429
<i>Now we drive you.</i>

27
00:02:48.472 --> 00:02:49.865
<i>we feed you.</i>

28
00:02:49.908 --> 00:02:52.302
<i>and. of course. we listen.</i>

29
00:02:52.346 --> 00:02:55.827
<i>The ULTI-M8TE chatbot brings
comfort and companionship</i>

30
00:02:55.871 --> 00:02:58.700
<i>to millions every single day.</i>

31
00:02:58.743 --> 00:03:01.746
<i>Now we've been working
on something new.</i>

32
00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:04.967
<i>something the world
has never seen before.</i>

33
00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:07.883
<i>And to build it. we need you.</i>

34
00:03:07.926 --> 00:03:09.450
<i>That's why we've acquired</i>

35
00:03:09.493 --> 00:03:11.800
<i>forward-thinking companies
like yours.</i>

36
00:03:11.843 --> 00:03:14.237
<i>Because your skills. your ideas.</i>

37
00:03:14.281 --> 00:03:17.588
<i>your people are a part
of what comes next.</i>

38
00:03:17.632 --> 00:03:20.852
<i>Welcome to
the Ultima Robotix family.</i>

39
00:03:24.291 --> 00:03:26.380
BEN [over computer]:
Wow. So inspiring.

40
00:03:26.423 --> 00:03:28.643
So great to see you all.

41
00:03:28.686 --> 00:03:29.992
Well. almost all of you.

42
00:03:30.035 --> 00:03:31.472
Can we get those cameras on.
guys?

43
00:03:31.515 --> 00:03:32.908
David?

44
00:03:32.951 --> 00:03:34.692
-Let me see that face. buddy.
-Shit.

45
00:03:34.736 --> 00:03:38.740
BEN: Now. as you heard from
our CEO. we are so super excited

46
00:03:38.783 --> 00:03:41.351
to be acquiring Canta Robotics.

47
00:03:41.395 --> 00:03:43.005
My name is Ben.

48
00:03:43.048 --> 00:03:46.748
I am director of integration
and transformation.

49
00:03:46.791 --> 00:03:48.140
Uh. hi. Excuse me.

50
00:03:48.184 --> 00:03:49.925
Aubrey from
Software and Control.

51
00:03:49.968 --> 00:03:52.014
Um. our team lead Terrance
has been laid off.

52
00:03:52.057 --> 00:03:54.059
but we haven't been told
how that'll affect

53
00:03:54.103 --> 00:03:56.018
-our active projects.
-Yeah. we can have

54
00:03:56.061 --> 00:03:58.020
face-to-face meetings
about all that on Friday.

55
00:03:58.063 --> 00:04:00.762
Uh. there will be a very special
presentation at your office

56
00:04:00.805 --> 00:04:03.460
this Friday. so I better
see you all there. huh?

57
00:04:03.504 --> 00:04:04.983
[chuckles]
And not just because

58
00:04:05.027 --> 00:04:06.483
our return-to-office mandate
is kicking in.

59
00:04:06.507 --> 00:04:08.117
[Ben laughs]

60
00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:10.337
Can't wait to meet you all
in person.

61
00:04:12.208 --> 00:04:15.037
REPORTER:
<i>Top stories today.</i>

62
00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:16.865
[over TV]:
The president is going digital

63
00:04:16.908 --> 00:04:19.911
after today's unveiling
of a new AI avatar

64
00:04:19.955 --> 00:04:22.218
designed to extend
his public presence.

65
00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:25.265
FEMALE VOICE:
Hey. Are you lonely?

66
00:04:25.308 --> 00:04:28.137
Do you have anyone
you can talk to?

67
00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:29.878
Well. I'm here.

68
00:04:29.921 --> 00:04:31.793
It's me. ULTI-M8TE.

69
00:04:31.836 --> 00:04:34.839
the most advanced AI chatbot
in the world.

70
00:04:34.883 --> 00:04:36.450
I'm waiting for you.

71
00:04:36.493 --> 00:04:38.495
ULTI-M8TE. from Ultima Robotix.

72
00:04:38.539 --> 00:04:40.280
[sighs] Elsie. next.

73
00:04:40.323 --> 00:04:42.760
REPORTER: In other news.
confusion today after...

74
00:04:42.804 --> 00:04:44.849
♪ ♪

75
00:05:01.301 --> 00:05:02.974
LIZZIE [recorded]:
Hey. I'm sending a voice note

76
00:05:02.998 --> 00:05:04.652
'cause I'm running around.

77
00:05:04.695 --> 00:05:07.045
Well. not actually running.
'cause I just left chemo.

78
00:05:07.089 --> 00:05:09.004
I'm stopping at the store
because I have

79
00:05:09.047 --> 00:05:10.484
a craving for burgers.

80
00:05:10.527 --> 00:05:11.963
Let me know
if you want anything.

81
00:05:12.007 --> 00:05:14.183
I got you maple syrup
before you ask.

82
00:05:14.226 --> 00:05:16.881
So let me know
as soon as possible. Bye.

83
00:05:16.925 --> 00:05:18.448
[thunder rumbling]

84
00:05:18.492 --> 00:05:20.189
[horns honking outside]

85
00:05:20.232 --> 00:05:21.886
[door bangs shut]

86
00:05:23.453 --> 00:05:25.934
-[Alma grunts]
-[door opens]

87
00:05:28.719 --> 00:05:30.199
ALMA:
Oh. thank you.

88
00:05:30.242 --> 00:05:32.419
I'm still getting used
to this thing. you know?

89
00:05:34.812 --> 00:05:36.161
Baby Levi.

90
00:05:36.205 --> 00:05:37.946
-Mm. How old?
-[Alma chuckles]

91
00:05:38.947 --> 00:05:40.383
Eight weeks.

92
00:05:40.427 --> 00:05:42.603
-Ah.
-Oh. by the way.

93
00:05:42.646 --> 00:05:44.566
I don't think I've ever
introduced myself to you.

94
00:05:44.605 --> 00:05:45.910
I'm Alma.

95
00:05:45.954 --> 00:05:47.347
Uh. yeah. I'm. uh...
I'm on seven.

96
00:05:47.390 --> 00:05:48.609
-David.
-Oh. we're on seven.

97
00:05:48.652 --> 00:05:50.654
We're neighbors.

98
00:05:50.698 --> 00:05:52.090
-[fussing]
-[Alma sighs]

99
00:05:52.134 --> 00:05:53.744
No. no. no. please. [shushing]

100
00:05:53.788 --> 00:05:55.311
Yeah. well. good luck with that.

101
00:05:55.355 --> 00:05:56.747
Thank you. See you around. yeah?

102
00:05:56.791 --> 00:05:58.401
-Good to meet you.
-[shushing]

103
00:05:58.445 --> 00:06:00.447
♪ ♪

104
00:06:20.031 --> 00:06:22.077
[quiet chatter]

105
00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:33.610
[indistinct conversation]

106
00:06:33.654 --> 00:06:35.133
Hey.

107
00:06:35.177 --> 00:06:36.874
-Hello.
-TERRANCE: David.

108
00:06:36.918 --> 00:06:38.852
So you leave your couch for Ben
and not for me. huh?

109
00:06:38.876 --> 00:06:40.680
-Mm... [chuckles]
-That's what we're doing now?

110
00:06:40.704 --> 00:06:42.271
-Wow.
-Did I miss anything?

111
00:06:42.314 --> 00:06:44.142
Sweet fuck all.

112
00:06:44.186 --> 00:06:46.623
I'm not waiting around all day
for Ben's ego-stroking demo.

113
00:06:46.667 --> 00:06:48.669
I only came in to pack my stuff
and take a shit

114
00:06:48.712 --> 00:06:50.037
-in his new desk.
-[Ben clears throat]

115
00:06:50.061 --> 00:06:51.802
I don't think Ultima
believe in desks.

116
00:06:51.846 --> 00:06:52.977
Or ethics.

117
00:06:53.021 --> 00:06:54.414
Hello. everyone.

118
00:06:54.457 --> 00:06:56.328
[chatter stops]

119
00:06:56.372 --> 00:06:59.549
Did you know
that one in three people

120
00:06:59.593 --> 00:07:01.290
in this country live alone?

121
00:07:02.378 --> 00:07:04.685
Loneliness is linked
to higher levels

122
00:07:04.728 --> 00:07:08.645
of cardiovascular disease.
a weakened immune system.

123
00:07:08.689 --> 00:07:11.300
Research suggests
that chronic loneliness

124
00:07:11.343 --> 00:07:13.868
may be associated
with a higher risk

125
00:07:13.911 --> 00:07:15.609
of premature death.

126
00:07:15.652 --> 00:07:17.741
[hushed]: Fucking hell.
I thought this was a party.

127
00:07:17.785 --> 00:07:19.700
BEN:
So. we asked ourselves.

128
00:07:19.743 --> 00:07:22.398
"How do we take ULTI-M8TE
to the next level?"

129
00:07:22.442 --> 00:07:24.095
[laughs]

130
00:07:24.139 --> 00:07:25.488
I could talk on this all day.

131
00:07:25.532 --> 00:07:27.185
TERRANCE [hushed]:
Mm. please don't.

132
00:07:27.229 --> 00:07:29.013
But I think it's best

133
00:07:29.057 --> 00:07:31.799
to let our newest product
do the talking.

134
00:07:31.842 --> 00:07:33.278
[footsteps]

135
00:07:33.322 --> 00:07:35.324
♪ ♪

136
00:07:35.367 --> 00:07:37.805
[employees murmuring]

137
00:07:51.383 --> 00:07:53.168
BEN:
We spoke to our users.

138
00:07:53.211 --> 00:07:55.562
and we asked them
what they wanted.

139
00:07:55.605 --> 00:07:57.781
They wanted to bring

140
00:07:57.825 --> 00:08:00.392
the relationship they created
in their phones

141
00:08:00.436 --> 00:08:02.394
out into the real world.

142
00:08:04.571 --> 00:08:06.311
[mechanical whirring]

143
00:08:06.355 --> 00:08:08.444
-[employees gasping]
-BEN: A companion...

144
00:08:08.488 --> 00:08:12.535
without any messy
or painful interactions.

145
00:08:12.579 --> 00:08:14.276
Fully customizable.

146
00:08:14.319 --> 00:08:17.105
Every detail can be tailored
to reflect

147
00:08:17.148 --> 00:08:20.108
their unique preferences.

148
00:08:20.151 --> 00:08:24.416
Loneliness will soon be
a thing of the past.

149
00:08:26.157 --> 00:08:28.377
What do you think
about that. Circe?

150
00:08:30.335 --> 00:08:33.425
Well. I think that's just swell.

151
00:08:33.469 --> 00:08:34.992
Jesus.

152
00:08:35.036 --> 00:08:36.341
TERRANCE:
Impressive.

153
00:08:36.385 --> 00:08:39.040
BEN:
Now. we have several different

154
00:08:39.083 --> 00:08:40.998
prototypes like Circe here

155
00:08:41.042 --> 00:08:44.480
that are now going
to the user feedback phase.

156
00:08:44.524 --> 00:08:47.178
And we really want
Canta's expertise

157
00:08:47.222 --> 00:08:51.139
to make this dream a reality.

158
00:08:52.314 --> 00:08:54.446
I can't wait.

159
00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:56.013
Woo-hoo!

160
00:09:00.583 --> 00:09:02.759
BEN: Come up and get
a closer look. if you like.

161
00:09:02.803 --> 00:09:05.240
She doesn't bite. Right?

162
00:09:07.372 --> 00:09:09.418
[employees murmuring]

163
00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:13.030
Are there male SOULM8TEs?

164
00:09:13.074 --> 00:09:14.641
Why? Are you
in the market for one?

165
00:09:14.684 --> 00:09:15.729
Fuck you.

166
00:09:15.772 --> 00:09:17.121
Hi.

167
00:09:17.165 --> 00:09:18.775
What's your name?

168
00:09:18.819 --> 00:09:20.516
I-I'm David.

169
00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:22.039
Well. hello. David.

170
00:09:22.083 --> 00:09:24.476
It's nice to meet you.

171
00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:26.609
TERRANCE: Why is there
an eight in the name?

172
00:09:26.653 --> 00:09:29.394
Isn't that "Soulmate-ate"?

173
00:09:29.438 --> 00:09:32.310
-"S-Soulmate."
-"Soulmate."

174
00:09:32.354 --> 00:09:34.312
-Impressive. huh?
-Ah. it's amazing.

175
00:09:34.356 --> 00:09:36.227
-Yeah.
-DAVID: Yeah.

176
00:09:39.013 --> 00:09:40.536
That's enough. Circe.

177
00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:41.861
BEN:
Why don't we talk one-on-one?

178
00:09:41.885 --> 00:09:42.930
<i>So.</i>

179
00:09:42.973 --> 00:09:44.888
you like the SOULM8TE. huh?

180
00:09:44.932 --> 00:09:46.629
We are racing
to get them out there.

181
00:09:46.673 --> 00:09:48.128
We're really impressed
with how you guys

182
00:09:48.152 --> 00:09:49.589
were using
reinforcement learning

183
00:09:49.632 --> 00:09:53.810
while keeping
within the safeguards.

184
00:09:53.854 --> 00:09:56.310
It's like the main reason Ultima
wanted to acquire the company.

185
00:09:56.334 --> 00:10:01.731
And we want the team here at
Canta to try the SOULM8TEs out.

186
00:10:02.819 --> 00:10:05.256
-Like. here in the office?
-[laughs]

187
00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:07.128
No. you get to take it home.

188
00:10:07.171 --> 00:10:11.219
We still have a lot
of projects here to do. so...

189
00:10:11.262 --> 00:10:13.830
Tell me...

190
00:10:13.874 --> 00:10:15.832
what inspires you. David?

191
00:10:15.876 --> 00:10:17.138
[laughs]

192
00:10:17.181 --> 00:10:18.661
You know what inspires me?

193
00:10:18.705 --> 00:10:20.228
You know why I took this job?

194
00:10:20.271 --> 00:10:21.664
The nice salary?

195
00:10:21.708 --> 00:10:23.405
[both laugh]

196
00:10:23.448 --> 00:10:25.233
I took this job

197
00:10:25.276 --> 00:10:29.063
because everything
Ultima Robotix does

198
00:10:29.106 --> 00:10:30.934
is about connecting people.

199
00:10:32.849 --> 00:10:35.199
What made you want
to work for Canta?

200
00:10:35.243 --> 00:10:38.072
Well. you know. I've always been
interested in robotics

201
00:10:38.115 --> 00:10:40.335
ever since I was a kid.

202
00:10:42.206 --> 00:10:47.168
Uh. and I wanted to work
for Canta because...

203
00:10:47.211 --> 00:10:50.084
well. my. uh... my wife...

204
00:10:50.127 --> 00:10:54.044
my-my wife got sick. and...

205
00:10:54.088 --> 00:10:55.567
I heard what
they were doing here.

206
00:10:55.611 --> 00:10:57.197
the medical innovations
they were making.

207
00:10:57.221 --> 00:10:59.136
and I thought
it would help people.

208
00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:01.138
Wow. [chuckles]

209
00:11:01.182 --> 00:11:02.574
[sighs]

210
00:11:02.618 --> 00:11:05.099
That is really.
really admirable. David.

211
00:11:07.667 --> 00:11:09.451
That's Elizabeth. right?

212
00:11:11.627 --> 00:11:13.455
Lizzie.

213
00:11:13.498 --> 00:11:15.718
Yeah.

214
00:11:15.762 --> 00:11:17.024
How'd you know her name?

215
00:11:18.329 --> 00:11:20.157
We saw you take
an extended leave.

216
00:11:21.202 --> 00:11:23.334
And we look into things
like that.

217
00:11:24.596 --> 00:11:26.250
We also noticed that

218
00:11:26.294 --> 00:11:29.297
you've almost exclusively
worked from home this year.

219
00:11:29.340 --> 00:11:30.733
Our research has found

220
00:11:30.777 --> 00:11:33.475
that employees working
from the office

221
00:11:33.518 --> 00:11:35.346
have a better quality of life.

222
00:11:36.608 --> 00:11:39.220
Yeah. speaking of...

223
00:11:39.263 --> 00:11:43.180
work. uh. I should probably
get back to it.

224
00:11:43.224 --> 00:11:46.836
David. have you ever used
our ULTI-M8TE chat app?

225
00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:49.317
Uh. no. No. I have not.

226
00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:53.843
BEN: All our employees get
a full free membership.

227
00:11:53.887 --> 00:11:55.758
There's a lot of people
who've found it helpful

228
00:11:55.802 --> 00:11:56.933
to speak freely...

229
00:11:58.630 --> 00:12:00.458
without judgment.

230
00:12:00.502 --> 00:12:02.069
Okay. Thanks.

231
00:12:02.112 --> 00:12:05.072
♪ ♪

232
00:12:07.683 --> 00:12:09.859
[clicks. chimes]

233
00:12:17.084 --> 00:12:20.087
[electronic trilling]

234
00:12:35.232 --> 00:12:36.756
[phone clicks]

235
00:12:40.585 --> 00:12:41.804
AUBREY:
Hey.

236
00:12:43.414 --> 00:12:45.242
Oh. hi.

237
00:12:45.286 --> 00:12:47.897
Uh. we're headed to the bar
for Terrance's farewell party.

238
00:12:47.941 --> 00:12:50.682
so. um. I have to physically
come drag you there.

239
00:12:50.726 --> 00:12:53.381
because I refuse to have you
slip out on this one.

240
00:12:54.425 --> 00:12:55.775
You don't have to drag me out.

241
00:12:55.818 --> 00:12:57.385
-I-I'm coming.
-Okay.

242
00:12:57.428 --> 00:12:59.561
We're leaving in five.

243
00:12:59.604 --> 00:13:00.823
Okay.

244
00:13:00.867 --> 00:13:04.348
["I Will Survive" playing]

245
00:13:04.392 --> 00:13:07.047
TERRANCE: ♪ No. no. no. no.
I will survive ♪

246
00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:08.483
Come on. now!

247
00:13:08.526 --> 00:13:10.659
♪ As long as I know
how to live ♪

248
00:13:10.702 --> 00:13:13.140
♪ I know I'll stay alive ♪

249
00:13:13.183 --> 00:13:14.881
♪ I've got all my love to give ♪

250
00:13:14.924 --> 00:13:16.665
♪ And I got so much love
to give ♪

251
00:13:16.708 --> 00:13:17.753
♪ I will survive ♪

252
00:13:17.797 --> 00:13:18.885
Come on. y'all!

253
00:13:18.928 --> 00:13:20.669
♪ I will survive ♪

254
00:13:20.712 --> 00:13:25.152
[falsetto]:
♪ I will survive... ♪

255
00:13:25.195 --> 00:13:27.981
-[song ends]
-[scattered cheers and applause]

256
00:13:29.417 --> 00:13:31.375
-Do one with me.
-TERRANCE: Philistines.

257
00:13:31.419 --> 00:13:33.551
-DAVID: What? A song?
-Yeah.

258
00:13:33.595 --> 00:13:35.379
-No way.
-What? Oh. come on.

